<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $57.3 mln Nov 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $57.3 mln Nov 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $57.3 million surplus on November 20 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 20</p>
<p>Exports: $265.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $246.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $357.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $320 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $57.3 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.329 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.356 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.094 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.303 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.764 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511-2485418</p>
